{"kind":"request","text":"ox-checker: independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of exact head c08aa0ff3d0d3a18e678ec5ccc06602bb3d28723 on branch request/mcp-review-tool (worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/mcp-review-tool), implementing request #9965, which asked for an MCP review tool guarded by the same validateReview floor the CLI uses, extracted once into a shared internal package.\n\nWHAT THE HEAD DOES. internal/reviewguard is new and holds the verdict guard exactly as cmd/gs held it: Validate (promise ownership, fingerprint independence, unique standing request basis, checkout checks) plus the standing/live statement-artifact helpers, staleness rendering, and the git runner; cmd/gs keeps one-line delegating wrappers so its call sites read as before. cmd/gitseq-mcp gains a review tool: it builds the same verdict body gs review builds (verdict, head, primary artifact, staleness when the world moved), rests it on promise + resolved request + every cited artifact, and files it through s.submit; every missing precondition refuses with a reason naming what is missing. docs/reference/mcp/review.md documents the tool with a runnable example.\n\nREPORTING ARTIFACTS. Exact-head artifacts rest on my promise #10021-ish (canonical id in rests_on): internal/reviewguard at git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d730ff3986ef49a75507cdc0452f010772978319 and cmd/gitseq-mcp at git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c512a27a8972b9cd0fb13ff7a5e1696f62f734bc. Successors were published and predecessors retired at cmd/gitseq-mcp (4 live), cmd/gs (3 live); first artifacts at internal/reviewguard and the new docs page.\n\nGATES ACTUALLY RUN at this head: gofmt -l . clean; go vet ./... clean; go test ./... -count=1 green; go test -race over cmd/gitseq-mcp and cmd/gs green; git diff --check clean; GOOS=windows go build ./... ok. Mutation check: disabling the shared independence clause fails a test at EACH call site - cmd/gs TestReviewGuardRefusesVerdictOnTheReviewersOwnArtifact and cmd/gitseq-mcp TestReviewToolRefusesWithTheReasonNamingWhatIsMissing - then restored. TestGateSurfaceCoversEveryMCPTool and the runnable-example gate are green with the new page.\n\nCONDITIONS FOR YOUR VERDICT. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and say whether this exact head preserves their contract - the extraction moves rules without changing them, and the tool surface grows by one entry with its reference page. Security: examine the trust and authority boundaries - the guard now serves two surfaces, so check that the MCP path cannot file what the CLI would refuse (independence by fingerprint, promise standing, canonical exact head, clean same-repo checkout) and that refusal reasons do not leak secrets; note the MCP path validates once rather than the CLI's twice-read, since build-then-sign is synchronous here. Simplification: identify any opportunity to simplify without weakening request #9965's conditions of satisfaction.","body":{"conditions":"Record three conclusions before any approval. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and say whether exact head c08aa0ff3d0d3a18e678ec5ccc06602bb3d28723 preserves or changes their contract. Security: examine the shared-guard trust boundary between the CLI and MCP filing surfaces, untrusted inputs (event ids, checkout path, verdict enum), independence enforcement by fingerprint, bounds on citations, and failure modes where validation and signing race; state the result and request changes for any unresolved defect. Simplification: identify any opportunity to simplify without weakening the conditions of satisfaction of request #9965; request changes to cut fluff.","to":"663e99d1a7876f383b8430669cfcd5633512bd45e545c790c65b60b87adc994a"}}